      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Audio Spectral Scrubbing: Cleaning Lyria and MusicLM SynthID Watermarks</h2>
    <p>
      Google Lyria and YouTube Dream Track utilize psychoacoustic watermarking to protect AI music compositions. SynthID for Audio embeds identification tones across specific harmonic frequencies that align with the human ear equal-loudness contours (Fletcher-Munson curves). Because human hearing cannot distinguish low-level energy changes beneath loudest masking tones, these watermarks survive MP3 compression and analogue microphone recordings.
    </p>
    <p>
      RemoveSynth tackles acoustic SynthID through adaptive spectral phase scrambling. By converting the time-domain waveform into the frequency domain via Fast Fourier Transform (FFT), our engine analyzes overlapping 2048-sample windows. Wherever phase coherence indicates artificial sinusoidal injection, the phase angle is randomized by a constrained delta (Delta theta &lt;= &plusmn; 0.05 rad), while the magnitude spectrum remains completely intact. The audio sounds 100 percent identical to the listener, but automated audio fingerprinters report negative detection scores.
    </p>

    <h2>Text De-biasing: Disrupting Statistical Tournament Sampling in LLM Outputs</h2>
    <p>
      When Google Gemini, Gemma, or Vertex AI text models output sentences, SynthID Text does not alter the text after generation. Instead, it biases the selection of tokens during generation. For every token position, the model hashes the preceding $h$ tokens to seed a pseudo-random value function $g(v) \in [0, 1]$. Tokens with high $g$-values are awarded probability boosts. Over long text passages (typically 300 words or more), the cumulative distribution of $g$-scores diverges sharply from natural language randomness.
    </p>
    <p>
      To neutralize SynthID Text signatures, RemoveSynth text sanitizer introduces controlled synonym replacement and syntactic restructuring at key hash anchor points. By substituting 1 in every 12 non-critical words with context-equivalent synonyms, the deterministic hash chain between n-grams is severed. The cumulative $g$-score collapses back to the expected null hypothesis distribution ($\mu = 0.50$), neutralizing algorithmic detection without modifying your factual meaning.
    </p>

